<title>USA: Philip Morris Q4 net shr $1.81 vs $1.53.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris Q4 net shr $1.81 vs $1.53.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>For fourth quarter ended December 31:</p>
<p>				    1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.81		    $1.53</p>
<p> Net			  1,471		    1,272</p>
<p> Operating revs	  16,736		   15,595</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	   813			834</p>
<p>For year ended December 31:</p>
<p> Shr primary		$7.68		    $6.48</p>
<p> Net			  6,303		    5,450</p>
<p> Operating revs	  68,938		   63,774</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	   821			842</p>
<p>(All data above in millions, except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 revenue is adjusted for divestitures. Unadjusted figures are $16.79 billion for 1996 quarter, compared with $15.74 billion in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>1996 full-year revenue also adjusted for divestitures. Unadjusted figures are $69.20 billion compared with $66.07 billion for 1995.</p>
<p>First CAll Q4 estimate was $1.80 per share.</p>
<p>Philip Morris Cos Inc is full company name.</p>
</text>
